    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d373">

                <pb facs="0374" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.842/141: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Italy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-03T14:00:00-04:00">August 3, 1936—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>100. Department’s 93, July 24, 4 p.m. Mr. Engert was officially informed on
                    August 2 that cipher communications between the legations in Addis Ababa and
                    their respective governments are now again permitted.</p>
                <p>In view of this favorable development the Department is not inclined to instruct
                    you to press the Italian Government at this time to permit our Legation to use
                    its radio for the transmission of messages.</p>
                <pb facs="0375" n="310" xml:id="pg310"/>
                <p>The Department would, however, be interested to receive any information that may
                    be discreetly obtainable as to the action, if any, contemplated in the latter
                    connection by any of your colleagues.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
